; FusionCut Pro packaging - Windows 8.x api-set forwarder stub.
;
; WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
;   librav1e.dll (the Rust-written AV1 encoder inside MSYS2's FFmpeg 8
;   dependency tree) hard-imports 'api-ms-win-core-synch-l1-2-0.dll' -
;   the WaitOnAddress futex API set - by its literal api-set name.
;
;   On Windows 10/11 the loader resolves that name via the ApiSetSchema
;   and redirects it to KernelBase before the file search runs; the
;   System32 placeholder stub is never touched.
;
;   On Windows 8/8.1 the loader does NOT schema-resolve this name. It
;   maps the System32 placeholder stub file, then reads that stub's
;   (empty/invalid) export data while snapping librav1e's imports -
;   dereferencing an unmapped page inside the stub image - and dies
;   with 0xC0000005 inside ntdll's loader code, BEFORE any user code
;   in the exe runs. The loader converts the fault into the process
;   exit status; Windows Error Reporting never engages; the user sees
;   only "The application was unable to start correctly (0xc0000005)"
;   with no Event Viewer entry and no log. (Diagnosed with
;   fcp-loader-check.exe v2's debug-launch watch: fault instruction in
;   ntdll+0x4b4b4, AV READ of an address inside the just-mapped
;   api-ms-win-core-synch-l1-2-0.dll image; load trail stopped at
;   avcodec-62 -> ... -> librav1e -> api-ms-win-core-synch-l1-2-0.)
;
; THE FIX
;   The DLL search order tries the application directory BEFORE
;   System32, so a real DLL with this exact name placed next to
;   FusionCutPro.exe wins the bind. This file defines that DLL: a
;   forwarder-only image with no code, no imports, and no CRT - just
;   an export table whose entries forward to the KernelBase
;   implementations (present since Windows 8). The loader reads OUR
;   valid export table, follows the forwarders into the already-loaded
;   KernelBase, and startup proceeds.
;
;   On Windows 10/11 this stub is inert (the schema resolves the name
;   before the file search), so shipping it everywhere is safe.
;
; BUILT IN CI (portable-build.yml) with:
;   gcc -shared -nostdlib \
;       -o dist/api-ms-win-core-synch-l1-2-0.dll \
;       packaging/api-ms-win-core-synch-l1-2-0.def
; and verified there with objdump (the export table must contain
; WaitOnAddress). The build sandbox has no MinGW/PE toolchain, so CI
; is the authoritative oracle for this artifact.

LIBRARY api-ms-win-core-synch-l1-2-0

EXPORTS
    Sleep               = kernelbase.Sleep
    WaitOnAddress       = kernelbase.WaitOnAddress
    WakeByAddressAll    = kernelbase.WakeByAddressAll
    WakeByAddressSingle = kernelbase.WakeByAddressSingle
